    statement: 'Read in full: the routine Ghidra calls FUN_00016ca0 (obj1+0x6ca0 to +0x6d67; called once from the race frame routine, race.frame-calls, at obj1+0x1fe91) sets three things for the race. (1) The steering rate word obj2+0x28c7c from the word obj2+0x28c20, the same word that picks between the floor routine\'s three variants (floor.render-loop): 0x28 for 1, 0x24 for 2, 0x20 for 3 (obj1+0x6cbe to +0x6cd4), replaced by 0x24 when the word obj2+0x28be2 or the dword obj2+0x1ec74 is non-zero (obj1+0x6cdd to +0x6cf0); the word obj2+0x28c7a is half of it (obj1+0x6d09 to +0x6d12) and obj2+0x28c54 is set to 0x78. These are the amounts the input routine adds to or subtracts from the heading each call (car.move-step; the hop and normal rates). (2) The 200-word active speed table at obj2+0x1e730 (car.speed-model, ai.race-speeds) is filled from the buffer at obj2+0x1e584 when the word obj2+0x1ea58 is 2 (obj1+0x6d0b to +0x6d34) and from the buffer at obj2+0x1e8c4 otherwise (obj1+0x6d3d to +0x6d59); those buffers hold VEL2.TAB and VEL.TAB (small.read, obs-buffers). So the slower curve is selected when that word is 2. (3) The dword obj2+0x1ed08, the command-line class (12, 6 or 0, cmdline.words and cmdline.class-one), is copied to obj2+0x1ea5c (obj1+0x6d5b). The two words are the full-screen detail level and the engine choice (setup.race-options). Not observed at run time.',
