    id: 'car.steer-states', tag: 'STATIC',
    statement: 'Read in full: the input routine Ghidra calls FUN_000224ec (obj1+0x124ec to +0x12bf2, called from the player control routine at obj1+0x197c9 when the car word +0xa is 0 and the terrain value is not 10) turns the key flags into the steering words of car.move-step. It does nothing unless the racer record word +0x6aae8 of the player is 0 and the word obj2+0x28c44 is 2 (obj1+0x124fe, +0x1250c). The flags are the words obj2+0x28b8c (set from the byte obj2+0x28cd5) and obj2+0x28b98 (from the byte obj2+0x28cdd) (obj1+0x19322 to +0x19344); the first leads to a decrease of the heading (the word obj2+0x28b92, anticlockwise as drawn with y down) and the second to an increase (obj2+0x28b90). (a) A forced turn: when the car word +6 is non-zero (obj1+0x1251f) the routine sets obj2+0x28b92 to 0x78 when +6 is 1, otherwise obj2+0x28b90 to 0x78, and clears the other, counts the word +8 up and, past 4, clears +6 and +0x3c (obj1+0x1252d to +0x1256f); so five calls turn the heading by 0x78 each. The control routine starts it (obj1+0x196db to +0x19750): with the car words +0xa, +0x3c, +0x20 and +6 all 0, the throttle +0x42 non-zero and the word obj2+0x28b46 set, it plays sound 0x11 and sets +6 to 1 when obj2+0x28b98 is 0 and to 2 when it is non-zero, +8 to 1 and +0x3c to the same 1 or 2. (b) A hop: while the car word +0x20 is non-zero (obj1+0x12574) and the global tick obj2+0x1ec64 has moved on from the word +0x32, the frame word +0x1a steps down for +0x20 equal to 1 (setting obj2+0x28b92 to the word obj2+0x28c54, 0x78) or up for the other value (setting obj2+0x28b90), and when it passes 0 or 0x10 the hop ends: +0x20, +0x22, +0x24 and the steering words are cleared and the throttle +0x42 is set to 0 (obj1+0x125bc to +0x1265e). (c) With +0x20 and +0x3c both 0 (obj1+0x12940 to +0x12998) the speed word +0x26 is lowered each call by (speed x the car dword +0x36) >> 16, to at least 0, where +0x36 is the SDX dword +0x120 of the surface (terrain.sdx-index), the same slowdown as ai.surface-slowdown; the throttle at 0x64 or more with +0x44 equal to 0, obj2+0x28be2 and obj2+0x1ec74 equal to 0 and the terrain value not 2 allows a hop or drift (obj1+0x1296e to +0x12998); the steering words then take the normal rate obj2+0x28c7c while a flag is set (obj1+0x129a7 to +0x129df), and counting the calls the flag has been held in +0x22 (decrease) or +0x24 (increase), the car starts a drift (+0x3c to 1 or 2, +0x40 to 0x78, frame +0x18 to 3 or 4, sound 0x11) when the count reaches the car word +0x3a, the SDX word +0x124 of the surface (obj1+0x12a02 to +0x12a47), or, when +0x3a is 0, starts a hop at once (+0x20 to 1 or 2, obj1+0x12a8b). (d) During a drift (+0x3c non-zero, obj1+0x12702) the steering words use half the rate (obj2+0x28c7a), the timer +0x40 falls by 10 a call and ends the drift when below 0 (obj1+0x128b0), and when the held count reaches +0x3e (twice +0x3a) the drift turns into a hop (obj1+0x127d1 to +0x12838). So a surface\'s SDX word +0x124 is the number of calls a steering key must be held at full throttle before the car slides, 0 meaning it hops at once, and its dword +0x120 slows the car every call. obj2+0x28b46 is button 4, the hand brake turn (input.buttons); the game\'s names for hop, drift and spin are not established here. Not observed at run time.',
